Found under k253 (ocp-worker, 2026-10-31). Apply lane. `ocp node add` reads neither gpu.enabled nor gpu.driver off the OCPNodeProvider CR: `_cli_reconcile` in lib/OCP/Cmd/Node/Add.pm passes only gpu_toolkit (k223) and, since k253, gpu_amd_integrated. robocop and `ocp apply`'s worker reconcile hand the whole flag set from OCP::Provider->gpu_flags_from_cr to OCP::Node. So on a node that `ocp node add` joins:
- the `gpu.enabled: false` kill switch does not hold -- detection runs;
- `gpu.driver: operator` does not hold -- host drivers get installed;
- since k253, `gpu.amd.integrated: true` opens the iGPU gate even on a cluster with gpu.enabled false.

The comment there says "gpu.enabled / gpu.driver have never been read on this path". Find out why (git log -S) before changing it: --gpu may be meant to override. Then either hand the whole set over, as the other join paths do (with --gpu's per-node opt-in on top), or write down why node add differs.

Done = node add's Rex params match robocop's for the same provider CR (a test on the t/253 model), with --gpu's own effect pinned; red first, then a mutation check.

